## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Applications of differentiation)
## DBsection(Newton's method)
## KEYWORDS("Newton's method", 'rootfinding')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## MLTleader(1)
## MLT(Newton-f-value)
## Level(2)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('4.1')
## Problem1('4')
#Problem APEX 4.1.4

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
Context('Numeric');

$a1 = random(2,5,1);
@x = (random(2.5,3.9,0.2));

$f = Formula("sin(x)");
$df = $f->D('x');

Context()->flags->set(  tolerance => 0.00001,  tolType => "absolute");

for my $k (0..4) {
    push(@x, $x[$k] - $f->eval(x => $x[$k])/$df->eval(x => $x[$k]));
}

BEGIN_PGML
Use 5 iterations of Newton's Method
with the given initial approximation to approximate
the root of the function.  All answers should be given
to 5 decimal digits of accuracy.

[```
   f(x) = \sin(x), \qquad x_0 = [$x[0]]
```]

- [` x_1 = `] [_]{$x[1]}{30}
- [` x_2 = `] [_]{$x[2]}{30}
- [` x_3 = `] [_]{$x[3]}{30}
- [` x_4 = `] [_]{$x[4]}{30}
- [` x_5 = `] [_]{$x[5]}{30}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Set up the iterative formula for Newton's Method:

[```
  x_{n+1} 
  = x_n - \frac{f(x_n)}{f'(x_n)} 
  = x_n - \frac{\sin x_n}{\cos x_n} = x_n - \tan x_n
```]

The iterations are:

[```
  \begin{aligned}
    x_0 &= [$x[0]] \\
    x_1 &= [$x[0]] - \tan [$x[0]] \approx [$x[1]] \\
    x_2 &= [$x[1]] - \tan [$x[1]] \approx [$x[2]] \\
    x_3 &= [$x[2]] - \tan [$x[2]] \approx [$x[3]] \\
    x_4 &= [$x[3]] - \tan [$x[3]] \approx [$x[4]] \\
    x_5 &= [$x[4]] - \tan [$x[4]] \approx [$x[5]]
  \end{aligned}
```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();

